================================================================================================================
THE GALAXY CEILING f_gal_max under three criteria
================================================================================================================
      All criteria are on the HALO-INJECTED scatter sigma_add = sqrt(rms(f)^2 - rms(0)^2), which is
      convention-free: it does not depend on this pipeline's absolute f=0 rms (0.142 dex L0 / 0.137 dex L2,
      reproducing the repository's committed L61/L92 gate numbers 0.145/0.142).
      C1 (ultra-loose) sigma_add <= 0.10 dex -- the halo may inject as much scatter as the ENTIRE observed RAR scatter
      C2 (headline)    sigma_add <= 0.06 dex -- the observed INTRINSIC-scatter budget (Lelli+2017, Li+2018)
      C3 (tight)       sigma_add <= 0.03 dex

          convention/profile/freedom  C1 add<0.10  C2 add<0.06  C3 add<0.03
  ('none' = that criterion is NEVER violated anywhere on the grid: it places NO ceiling on f at all)
                    ('AM', 'NFW', 0)        none        0.2674       0.0289
                    ('AM', 'NFW', 2)        none        0.6278       0.0391
                ('AM', 'Burkert', 2)        none        0.6664       0.0897
                    ('CS', 'NFW', 0)        none         none        0.3484
                    ('CS', 'NFW', 2)        none         none         none 
                ('CS', 'Burkert', 2)        none         none         none 
      
      HEADLINE  f_gal_max (AM halo, NFW, MOST forgiving L2 freedom, C2 criterion) = 0.6278
      LOOSEST   f_gal_max over every convention/profile/criterion               = NO CEILING (criterion never violated)
      KEY STRUCTURAL RESULT: with a0 honestly refit, the RAR-scatter criterion at the ultra-loose
      0.10 dex level is NEVER violated -- because the best-fit a0 slides to zero and the model morphs
      continuously into mean-relation LCDM.  The RAR scatter therefore does NOT by itself bound f;
      the binding constraint must come from elsewhere (see L149).
  [PASS] the galaxy ceiling is resolved inside the scanned grid, not an extrapolation   (f_gal_max = 0.6278)
  [PASS] GUARD  giving the fit MORE freedom (L0 -> L2 per-galaxy Upsilon) RAISES the ceiling, i.e. the constraint is not an artefact of withheld freedom   (L0 0.2674 -> L2 0.6278)
  [PASS] GUARD  the a0 refit is actually active (a0 falls as f rises), so no spurious kill from a frozen a0   (a0/a0_can: 1.211 at f=0 -> 0.004 at f=1)
  [PASS] the CS 'cosmic share' convention is WEAKER than the AM convention (mass-independent ratio is nearly degenerate with a0), as expected   (CS inf vs AM 0.6278)
      kernel insensitivity (AM/NFW/L0): nu_RAR: rms 0.1421->0.1471->0.1528; bounded_boost: rms 0.1421->0.1471->0.1528
  [PASS] the halo-injected scatter at f=0.05 is KERNEL-INSENSITIVE (the result is not an artefact of one interpolating function)   (injected sigma at f=0.05: nu_RAR 0.0378 vs bounded_boost 0.0378 dex)
      gas-dominated subsample (M_gas > M_star): 66 galaxies -- stellar M/L freedom cannot hide a halo here

